 of [unclassified numerical context withheld]- exo -hydroxycamphor was established by GC-MS comparison with an authentic standard ( Fig. [unclassified numerical context withheld] ). The T252N and T252N/V253T mutants, like the wild-type protein, showed strong camphor hydroxylation activities. However, as previously reported [ [unclassified numerical context withheld] ], the camphor hydroxylation activity of the T252A mutant was negligible ( Fig. [unclassified numerical context withheld] ). These results suggest that the function of the highly conserved Thr residue can be satisfied by an asparagine. ","end":67572,"representation":"original","source_ref":"source_aac119387c3e0c2362e548a1","start":66776,"status":"numerical_scope_unresolved","unavailable_reason":"unrequested_numerical_scope_unresolved"}],"value":"chemically_identified"},"same_molecule":{"support":[{"artifact_ref":"artifact_fe5ba79bc3152f6d94f730cc7e02b43c041fbcb5092afa434386ba3c60c2e7de","display_text":"[Mixed numerical source context retained; requested operand scope unresolved.]  \n Wild-type \n [unrequested numerical operand] \n [unrequested numerical operand] \n [unclassified numerical context withheld] \n [unclassified numerical context withheld] \n [unrequested numerical operand] \n ","end":74525,"representation":"original","source_ref":"source_aac119387c3e0c2362e548a1","start":74203,"status":"numerical_scope_unresolved","unavailable_reason":"unrequested_numerical_scope_unresolved"}],"value":"same"},"same_preparation":{"support":[],"value":"unknown"},"source_pairing":{"support":[{"artifact_ref":"artifact_fe5ba79bc3152f6d94f730cc7e02b43c041fbcb5092afa434386ba3c60c2e7de","display_text":"[Mixed numerical source context retained; requested operand scope unresolved.]  The rates of H [unclassified numerical context withheld] O [unclassified numerical context withheld]  formation and NADH consumption were measured to calculate the coupling efficiency of the wild-type and P450  cam   mutants. In our assays, the wild-type P450  cam   exhibited a coupling efficiency of [unclassified numerical context withheld]% as judged by comparison of NADH consumption and 5-hydroxycamphor formation ( Table [unclassified numerical context withheld] ). The T252N and T252N/V253T mutants had coupling efficiencies of [unclassified numerical context withheld]% and [unclassified numerical context withheld]%, respectively ( Table [unclassified numerical context withheld] ). With none of these three enzymes was the formation of H [unclassified numerical context withheld] O [unclassified numerical context withheld]  detected, which suggests that the uncoupling occurred after oxygen activation to produce water. The T252A mutant, in contrast, exhibited a high rate of NADH consumption and the production of both H [unclassified numerical context withheld] O [unclassified numerical context withheld]  and H [unclassified numerical context withheld] O, but no camphor hydroxylation. These results indicate that the asparagine substitution allowed the enzyme to oxidize the substrate with an efficiency and rate approaching that of the wild-type enzyme. ","end":72886,"representation":"original","source_ref":"source_aac119387c3e0c2362e548a1","start":71815,"status":"numerical_scope_unresolved","unavailable_reason":"unrequested_numerical_scope_unresolved"}],"value":"author_assigned"}},"sheet_ref":"source_39012d9481adbe220d091f22","source_exact_value":{"denominator":"1","numerator":"206"},"source_kind":"primary_source","source_meanings":{"blank":null,"calibration":null,"cofactor_conditions":{"artifact_ref":"artifact_fe5ba79bc3152f6d94f730cc7e02b43c041fbcb5092afa434386ba3c60c2e7de","display_text":"[Mixed numerical source context retained; requested operand scope unresolved.]  NADH oxidation rates for P450  cam   enzymes were determined in steady state kinetic experiments using the P450/Pd/PdR system in a [unclassified numerical context withheld]:[unclassified numerical context withheld]:[unclassified numerical